WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.840
Welcome back.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.263
You've worked John Doe versus Robert Smith for five days now,

00:00:06.263 --> 00:00:11.470
from the intake call on February 9th, 2026, all the way to the closing letter.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.940
There's nothing new to learn today.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.071
We're going to sit down together and talk the file through the way a good team does

00:00:19.071 --> 00:00:23.162
after a case closes: where the money went, where the traps were hidden,

00:00:23.162 --> 00:00:26.330
and where a lot of files, maybe yours, went off course.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.520
Nobody is being graded.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:33.110
If you notice something in your own work and think, I did that, good.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.620
That's the point.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.157
Every figure and date I give you comes from the case file,

00:00:38.157 --> 00:00:40.850
so you can check each one against what you built.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.000
Before we go on, set yourself up.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.544
Open your CMS file for John Doe, your Net Sheet,

00:00:49.544 --> 00:00:53.070
both tracks if you built both, and your Lien Tracker.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.317
Every time I put a figure on the screen, pause the video and find the same figure in

00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:58.900
your file.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.530
If yours matches, move on.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.760
If it doesn't, don't just overwrite it.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.630
Ask two questions.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.620
Where did my number come from?

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.450
And which document proves the right one?

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.755
Most wrong figures on this file started in a draft or a provider's statement and got

00:01:16.755 --> 00:01:17.640
copied forward.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.710
So fix it where it started, with a dated note that cites the source.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.565
And one rule for the whole session: anything about what the case is worth,

00:01:26.565 --> 00:01:29.792
or which way to go, is Attorney Elijah Thorne's call,

00:01:29.792 --> 00:01:30.340
not ours.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.010
We'll come back to that line near the end.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.200
First, the whole file in one picture.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:45.585
On February 6th, 2026, John Doe was the front-seat passenger in Kevin Alvarez's 2020

00:01:45.585 --> 00:01:46.590
Ford Escape.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:52.153
Robert Smith, driving a Silverado, did not stop at the all-way stop and struck the

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:54.060
Escape's front passenger door.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.730
John owns no car and has no auto policy of his own.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.600
That drives the whole coverage picture.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.550
He didn't treat until February 20th, 14 days later.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:09.340
Then, after a good start, his care stopped for 19 days in April.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.370
Both facts come back again and again.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.400
Then the file forks.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:21.590
On Track A, the file settles before suit, and money goes out on October 22nd, 2026.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.959
On Track B, Keystone stonewalls at 3,500 dollars,

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:30.141
Attorney Thorne files suit on September 24th, 2026,

00:02:30.141 --> 00:02:34.570
and the file ends in arbitration, disbursed July 30th,

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:34.980
2027.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.370
Same 40,000 dollars gross on both tracks.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.440
Very different nets.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.590
We'll see exactly why.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.580
First stop on the money trail: what counts as recovery.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.770
Here's where a lot of files went wrong on Day 1.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.760
The stack is three layers, taken in order.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.350
Keystone's BI, 10,000 dollars.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.820
Then Harbor Point's Host UM, 20,000 dollars, because John rode in the Escape.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:08.633
Then Cardinal State's Relative UM, 10,000 dollars,

00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:14.173
because he lives with his mother, Margaret, and it sits as excess over the first

00:03:14.173 --> 00:03:14.450
two.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.120
That's 40,000 dollars.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:22.796
If your Coverage Stack came to 50,000, you almost certainly put PIP inside it as a

00:03:22.796 --> 00:03:23.510
fourth row.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.140
PIP and MedPay pay bills while the claim is open.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.410
They are never part of the gross.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.593
Keystone's property damage payments are for Margaret's parked Civic,

00:03:33.593 --> 00:03:34.720
not John's recovery.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:40.775
And Bluewater is not a fourth layer: Margaret rejected UM on that policy in writing

00:03:40.775 --> 00:03:42.150
on March 14th, 2024.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.100
One more point on order.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:50.619
UM owes nothing until BI is exhausted, so a UM demand before the BI tender was

00:03:50.619 --> 00:03:51.410
premature.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:58.243
And when Harbor Point offered 8,000 dollars, saying BI had already compensated him,

00:03:58.243 --> 00:04:02.305
the answer was in the file: its letter of March 2nd,

00:04:02.305 --> 00:04:06.836
2026 says its UM is add-on, not reduced by the BI payment,

00:04:06.836 --> 00:04:08.320
with no PIP offset.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:14.670
Never net BI or PIP out of a UM limit, on your stack or on your Net Sheet.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.900
Now PIP, and this is where the money trail really starts.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.890
Harbor Point's add-on PIP on the Escape is 10,000 dollars.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:31.190
But in Riverton, the full medical benefit opens only when a physician documents an

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.880
Emergency Medical Condition.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:37.030
Without that finding, PIP stops at 2,500 dollars.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:43.644
On our file, Dr. Sarah Spine documented the EMC at Riverton General's emergency

00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:46.340
department on February 20th, 2026.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.170
So treat that record as a money document.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.800
If your PIP Log doesn't show it, 7,500 dollars of benefits had nothing behind them.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:03.550
The ER billed 24,400 dollars and PIP paid 8,850 dollars at the fee schedule.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:11.940
EMS billed 2,182 dollars and 60 cents and PIP paid 1,150 dollars.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:17.370
Both paid on March 4th, 2026, and that's the whole 10,000.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.686
If your file shows PIP money left after that date,

00:05:21.686 --> 00:05:25.732
or PIP paying the urgent care, Lakeside or the MRI,

00:05:25.732 --> 00:05:27.080
go back and look.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.710
That was MedPay.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.180
And the 14-day treatment condition is Florida's rule, not Riverton's.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:41.916
Once PIP ran out, the next payer was MedPay, 5,000 dollars on the same Harbor Point

00:05:41.916 --> 00:05:44.450
policy, paid at the billed amount.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:51.080
The order is PIP, then MedPay, then Peach State, then the LOP.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.590
Skipping MedPay, or putting it first, is the slip to look for in your Day 2 work.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:03.224
MedPay paid in date order: the urgent care's 685 dollars on March 9th,

00:06:03.224 --> 00:06:09.419
Lakeside's first visit at 640 dollars, Summit's MRI at 2,395 dollars,

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:13.100
and two more Lakeside visits at 640 each.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:18.650
That's 5,000 dollars, gone on June 26th, 2026.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.720
Check your notes on this one.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:24.310
On March 11th, Summit asked for a Letter of Protection.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:31.500
If you said yes, you turned a covered bill into a 2,395 dollar lien on John's net.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.770
MedPay still had money, so the answer was no.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.254
The only LOP on this file is Riverton Spine and Rehab,

00:06:39.254 --> 00:06:44.920
signed February 23rd, 2026, because it was out of network for Peach State.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:53.010
Peach State is the health plan, and its notice of reimbursement rights came on

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.430
February 27th, 2026.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.489
That's the day the lien gets flagged in the CMS,

00:06:57.489 --> 00:06:59.860
not months later when the ledger shows up.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:05.570
On June 10th, its interim ledger asserted 3,618 dollars.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.320
If that number made it into your Lien Tracker as the lien, here's why it's wrong.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:15.950
The plan claimed Crescent's injection at the billed 3,400 dollars,

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.190
when it actually paid 1,860.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.527
And it swept in three lines that have nothing to do with the crash:

00:07:22.527 --> 00:07:26.156
an eye exam on February 3rd, three days before the collision,

00:07:26.156 --> 00:07:30.500
a sinusitis visit, and an allergy visit for a condition John already had.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.370
A plan can claim back only what it paid for the collision's care.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:41.241
The dispute went out in writing on June 12th, and the corrected itemization of June

00:07:41.241 --> 00:07:43.520
24th confirmed 1,860 dollars.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.630
The plan's cover letter asks for the full amount, without reduction.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.780
That's their opening position, not the answer.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:56.010
The plan is fully insured, a fact you record from its own notice and certificate.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:59.553
Which law governs the reduction, and the reduction itself,

00:07:59.553 --> 00:08:01.040
are Attorney Thorne's call.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:08.696
Now the Specials, and this is where I'd ask you to pause and look hard at your own

00:08:08.696 --> 00:08:09.070
audit.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:18.340
Riverton Spine and Rehab's LOP ledger shows 34 lines at 185 dollars, 6,290 dollars.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:24.410
The attendance log shows 33 visits: 16 before the disruption and 17 after it.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:28.200
May 4th, 2026 is billed twice.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:34.220
If your medical total came to 41,585 dollars, you added the statement instead of

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.070
auditing it.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:40.481
The audited medical is 41,400 dollars, and the removal should be visible,

00:08:40.481 --> 00:08:43.740
with its date and amount, not dropped silently.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:49.064
Add the wages, 9 shifts at 8 hours at 22 dollars,

00:08:49.064 --> 00:08:54.850
1,584 dollars, and the Total Specials are 42,984 dollars.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.360
Watch the digits.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:09:00.590
The draft demand typed 42,894.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:07.150
And the draft UM demands put Dr. Reyes's future care inside the Specials to reach

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.300
46,384 dollars.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:14.170
Future medical, 3,400 to 6,800 dollars, belongs in the narrative.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.801
Finally, the clinic won't reissue its ledger until the account closes,

00:09:18.801 --> 00:09:21.920
so the audited figure stands on the attendance log.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:28.470
Here's a column a lot of files left out: what was actually paid.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:33.300
Some dropped it to keep the number high; others picked the paid figure themselves.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.290
Neither is ours to do.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.560
Show billed and paid side by side.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.310
PIP paid 10,000 dollars.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.580
MedPay paid 5,000.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.890
Peach State paid 1,860.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:50.560
The LOP balance owed is 6,105.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:55.350
And John paid 312 dollars and 40 cents himself at Riverton Drug.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:10:00.580
That column comes to 23,277 dollars and 40 cents.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:08.281
Tie it back: 41,400 dollars of bills, less 16,582 dollars and 60 cents of PIP

00:10:08.281 --> 00:10:15.250
fee-schedule write-offs, less Crescent's 1,540 dollar contract write-off.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:19.240
If your columns don't tie, something is missing or counted twice.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.390
That 1,540 is a trap too.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:27.580
Crescent's patient statement billed it to John, and an in-network provider can't.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.893
If your file shows it as owed, fix it at the source:

00:10:31.893 --> 00:10:38.219
an Amendment Request to Renee Halvorsen, and the corrected zero-dollar statement of

00:10:38.219 --> 00:10:40.810
July 10th, 2026 goes in Exhibit E.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.840
It's never a lien and never John's bill.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:52.590
And don't quote 23,277 as the medical total, or the 42,984 as what was paid.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:56.840
Which column goes in the demand is Attorney Thorne's call under the

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.460
collateral-source rule that governs the case.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.570
Let's do Track A's Net Sheet to the cent.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.480
Gross 40,000 dollars.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:13.750
The fee is one third pre-suit, 13,333 dollars and 33 cents.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:21.260
If you typed 33.33 percent, you got 13,332 dollars, and that's a real error.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:25.650
Costs are 486 dollars and 75 cents, all receipted.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:31.240
Peach State came down to 1,240 dollars, accepted October 9th.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:37.119
Riverton Spine and Rehab came down from the audited 6,105 to 4,580,

00:11:37.119 --> 00:11:40.750
with a signed Payoff Letter on October 12th.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.300
Net to John: 20,359 dollars and 92 cents.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.290
Now the two streams.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:54.280
Costs and liens are split pro rata to the gross, 25 and 75 percent, charged once.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.470
Now go back to your October 6th sheet.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:04.577
On that date the liens were not reduced yet, so stream two is a projection:

00:12:04.577 --> 00:12:07.100
13,661 dollars and 19 cents.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:11.309
If it already showed 15,269 dollars and 94 cents,

00:12:11.309 --> 00:12:15.010
you entered reductions nobody had accepted yet.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:20.653
If it showed 11,548 dollars and 25 cents, you charged all the costs and both

00:12:20.653 --> 00:12:25.040
unreduced liens to the UM stream because it's the bigger check.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.030
Only written acceptances go on the sheet.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:35.420
Track B starts from the same 40,000 dollars, so why does John net less?

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:40.540
While Keystone held at 3,500 dollars, its BI layer wasn't exhausted,

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:44.890
and that froze the whole stack behind a 10,000 dollar carrier.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:51.829
Suit was filed September 24th, 2026, so the retainer's 40 percent tier applies:

00:12:51.829 --> 00:12:53.080
16,000 dollars.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.760
Costs grow to 3,895 dollars and 25 cents with the filing fee,

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:02.160
the process server, half the mediator, the arbitrator's share,

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.070
the court reporter and certified records.

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:09.930
Peach State's reduction follows the fee actually charged,

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.620
744 dollars off, so 1,116 dollars.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:17.050
Riverton Spine and Rehab settles at 4,275.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:26.660
Net 14,713 dollars and 75 cents, which is 5,646 dollars and 17 cents less than Track

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:26.880
A.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:32.533
If your Track B sheet still showed one third, or 1,240 for Peach State,

00:13:32.533 --> 00:13:34.550
you reused Track A's sheet.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.180
Each track is its own file.

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:39.770
And whether suing was worth it?

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:44.000
That conversation with John is Attorney Thorne's, never ours.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.350
Now the traps that were planted in the documents.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.020
A draft is not a source.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:56.210
Start with the BI demand draft, RS33.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:03.960
Its total reads 42,894 dollars, but the lines add to 42,984.

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:09.670
It counts 30 days from the letter's own date, July 20th, and writes August 19th.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:16.006
The clock really runs from Dana Whitfield's written acknowledgement on July 22nd,

00:14:16.006 --> 00:14:18.740
so the deadline is August 21st, 2026.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:23.658
With no written acknowledgement, you follow up the same day and escalate to Attorney

00:14:23.658 --> 00:14:26.050
Thorne; you never docket from the send date.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:29.768
It offers a full and final release of all claims,

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:33.755
which in our own demand would release the two UM carriers,

00:14:33.755 --> 00:14:35.680
30,000 dollars of the stack.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:39.310
And Robert Smith's affidavit of no other insurance is missing.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:43.833
The UM drafts, RS61, put future medical inside the Specials,

00:14:43.833 --> 00:14:49.120
demanded Relative UM as if it were primary, and filled in their own response

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:52.180
deadline, which is Attorney Thorne's to set.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.850
They never answered the gap or the degenerative reading, either.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:01.479
And the exhibit packet, RS66, had ten faults, including the wrong police report

00:15:01.479 --> 00:15:05.755
number, the attorney-only case summary, Margaret's car estimate,

00:15:05.755 --> 00:15:07.760
and no Gap Explanation Record.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.990
This one would have paid John's money away.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:18.386
On Track B, the Litigation Desk's draft arbitration binder,

00:15:18.386 --> 00:15:21.380
RS63, had a Lien Sheet at line C-9.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:29.961
It listed Harbor Point PIP at 10,000 dollars, plus Peach State at 1,860 and Riverton

00:15:29.961 --> 00:15:34.370
Spine and Rehab at 6,105, for 17,965 dollars.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:40.415
Harbor Point's add-on PIP has no reimbursement right under Riverton law,

00:15:40.415 --> 00:15:44.845
and Harbor Point confirmed that in writing on March 2nd,

00:15:44.845 --> 00:15:45.240
2026.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.710
PIP paying a bill doesn't create a lien.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:52.660
And Harbor Point is the carrier across the table at that hearing.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:57.248
The audited sheet, RS70, shows 7,965 dollars owed,

00:15:57.248 --> 00:16:01.654
Peach State plus Riverton Spine and Rehab, with PIP,

00:16:01.654 --> 00:16:06.570
MedPay, Summit and Crescent at zero, each with its source.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:11.249
It stays in Attorney Thorne's set, never exchanged and never shown to the

00:16:11.249 --> 00:16:13.680
arbitrator, but it still has to be right.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.790
The difference is exactly 10,000 dollars.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:23.764
Had only the 10,000 dollar BI come in, 6,179 dollars and 92 cents would be left

00:16:23.764 --> 00:16:28.460
after the fee and costs, against 7,965 dollars of liens.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:34.467
Shared pro rata, Peach State gets 1,443 dollars and 15 cents,

00:16:34.467 --> 00:16:39.290
Riverton Spine and Rehab 4,736 dollars and 77 cents,

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.330
and John gets nothing.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.640
Every lien dollar you overstate comes out of his share.

00:16:44.990 --> 00:16:47.190
Not every payer is a lienholder.

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:52.288
Before anything goes on the payables, ask whether that payer has a written right to

00:16:52.288 --> 00:16:52.860
be repaid.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.290
Now the common mistakes, day by day.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.520
Check your CMS intake.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:05.950
It came keyed with John as the driver and a date of birth of August 14th, 1990.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:09.060
He was the passenger, born in 1991.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:14.530
Driver isn't a small typo: passenger status is what opens both UM layers.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.939
The intake sheet also transposed the police report number,

00:17:17.939 --> 00:17:22.000
and that same wrong number showed up months later in the draft demand packet.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.840
On the letters of representation, Cardinal State had no adjuster yet,

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:31.264
so it goes to the Claims Department, and each UM letter is a notice,

00:17:31.264 --> 00:17:32.110
not a demand.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:37.460
Keystone's limit stays preliminary until its declarations page arrives March 20th.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:41.618
On the calendar, February 6th, 2028 is a Sunday,

00:17:41.618 --> 00:17:48.203
so we never rely on a weekend roll-forward: the internal hard date is February 4th,

00:17:48.203 --> 00:17:52.170
2028, and the filing cutoff is November 5th, 2027.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:56.259
And John's HIPAA authorization expires February 6th,

00:17:56.259 --> 00:17:58.920
2027, right in the middle of Track B.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:05.670
On the 14-day gap, did you ask, was it because you had no car?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.220
That's leading.

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:10.450
Ask open questions and write down his words.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:14.764
The reasons were no transport, soreness he thought would pass,

00:18:14.764 --> 00:18:17.960
worry about cost, and numbness from February 18th.

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:23.294
On the April disruption, if your notes say non-compliant or lost interest,

00:18:23.294 --> 00:18:26.190
that's the defense's story, not the file's.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:31.660
The cause was crash-related anxiety, documented by Dr. Reyes on April 20th.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.250
Now wages.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:38.066
John's own worksheet said 1,760 dollars, built from memory,

00:18:38.066 --> 00:18:40.640
with overtime that never happened.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:45.950
Northgate's records give 9 shifts, 1,584 dollars.

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.746
The five February shifts have no doctor's note,

00:18:48.746 --> 00:18:51.140
so keep them and flag them to Attorney Thorne.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:56.015
PIP's 80 percent wage benefit, 1,267 dollars and 20 cents,

00:18:56.015 --> 00:19:00.617
was never payable, because the limit was gone on March 4th,

00:19:00.617 --> 00:19:04.050
long before Northgate's letter on June 30th.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:07.933
And if a record is wrong, like the MRI's injury date,

00:19:07.933 --> 00:19:10.400
the provider corrects it by addendum.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.590
We never change it ourselves.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:18.940
Keystone's draft release discharged all other persons and insurers.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:22.973
Signed, it would have released Harbor Point and Cardinal State,

00:19:22.973 --> 00:19:24.610
30,000 dollars of the stack.

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:28.257
The same draft released Property Damage and Loss of Use,

00:19:28.257 --> 00:19:32.849
Margaret's open claim, and its confidentiality clause would have kept you from

00:19:32.849 --> 00:19:35.440
showing the UM carriers proof of exhaustion.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:41.670
It made John indemnify and defend against liens, and it reserved no UM claims.

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:46.777
Your clause review on August 14th goes to Attorney Thorne with every one of them

00:19:46.777 --> 00:19:50.225
listed; the Limited Release of August 19th fixed them all,

00:19:50.225 --> 00:19:53.020
and nothing was signed before both UM consents.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:59.872
On October 14th, Vance and Kettering claimed 6,666 dollars and 67 cents on an

00:19:59.872 --> 00:20:02.490
agreement only Margaret signed.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:07.160
Calling that lien invalid is a legal conclusion, not ours.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:12.521
Log it, route it the same day, hold the money on Attorney Thorne's instruction,

00:20:12.521 --> 00:20:13.790
and build the facts.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:18.300
Checks wait for cleared funds and signed Payoff Letters, never a phone call.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.410
On the litigation calendar, count every rule.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:26.554
Discovery mailed December 1st is 30 days plus 3 for mail,

00:20:26.554 --> 00:20:30.591
January 3rd, 2027, a Sunday, so it's due Monday,

00:20:30.591 --> 00:20:31.600
January 4th.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:37.750
Our expert disclosure is March 15th, 2027, not the defense's April 15th.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:41.660
And the Saturday brief date moves back to Friday, June 11th.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:48.809
Let's talk about the line, because a lot of the mistakes we just covered were not

00:20:48.809 --> 00:20:49.490
math errors.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:53.280
They were someone deciding something that wasn't theirs to decide.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:57.916
When Attorney Thorne asked, what do you think we should demand,

00:20:57.916 --> 00:21:01.521
the right answer was the inputs: the limits in order,

00:21:01.521 --> 00:21:04.990
the 42,984 dollars of Specials, the future medical.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.500
Not a number.

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:11.396
When a lienholder pushed for a quick answer, the right answer was,

00:21:11.396 --> 00:21:16.010
I'll take that to Attorney Thorne, not a reduction agreed by phone.

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:19.375
When John asked whether he should take 3,500 dollars,

00:21:19.375 --> 00:21:22.332
or whether suing was worth it, the right answer was,

00:21:22.332 --> 00:21:26.200
that's a question for your attorney, and I'll set up the call today.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.550
One more thing about roles.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:33.975
The case manager on a litigated file isn't always the person who ran it in pre-lit;

00:21:33.975 --> 00:21:37.460
in litigation, the case manager is usually the paralegal.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:43.210
On our file, the filing set went to the Litigation Desk paralegal, Nadia Brooks.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:47.522
So before you transfer a file, log an update or route a call,

00:21:47.522 --> 00:21:51.160
check who's assigned in the CMS and on the Case Profile.

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:56.087
Our job is to make every fact in the file true and every deadline safe,

00:21:56.087 --> 00:21:59.310
and then hand it to the person licensed to decide.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:03.700
A clean, sourced file is what lets him argue for John with confidence.

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:07.610
Here's your checklist.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:11.440
Pause the video now and check each row against your file.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:16.870
Rather than read the table to you, I'll name the rows that trip files up, and why.

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:21.413
A gross of 50,000 means PIP got counted as a layer;

00:22:21.413 --> 00:22:26.100
PIP and MedPay pay bills, they never add to the recovery.

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:32.483
Specials of 42,894 means you copied the draft demand's typo instead of adding the

00:22:32.483 --> 00:22:32.930
lines.

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:38.813
Liens of 17,965 mean the draft binder's PIP line is still on your sheet,

00:22:38.813 --> 00:22:42.040
and that's 10,000 dollars of John's money.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:49.230
A Track A fee of 13,332 means you typed 33.33 percent instead of one third.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:52.660
And PIP money after March 4th was really MedPay.

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:56.410
When a row reads differently, don't just retype it.

00:22:56.760 --> 00:23:00.800
Write down where your number came from and which document gives the right one.

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:05.830
That note is the real learning, and it's what you'll bring to your companion case.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:09.500
Let's close.

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:12.930
If you take three things from this file, take these.

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:16.080
First, a draft is not a source.

00:23:16.430 --> 00:23:21.540
The demand drafts, the binder, the provider ledger and the plan's interim ledger all

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:26.041
had errors, and every one of them was caught by going back to the document

00:23:26.041 --> 00:23:26.710
underneath.

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:30.060
Second, every dollar traces to a document.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:35.144
The EMC record, the PIP and MedPay ledger, the attendance log and the signed

00:23:35.144 --> 00:23:38.570
acceptances are what made John's net right to the cent.

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:43.640
Third, decisions about value and strategy belong to Attorney Thorne.

00:23:43.990 --> 00:23:47.670
Your companion case will have the same traps under different names.

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:51.460
Thank you for the work you put into John Doe's file this week.

00:23:51.810 --> 00:23:56.050
Now go fix whatever you found today, at the source, and write down why.

